Message-ID: <5de987f148336a80bea1fea05d78b58fe82b7d75.1776946505.git.bertrand.marquis@arm.com>
In-Reply-To: <55d56a174a0f04520d4a1558630bb0b739074b13.1776946505.git.bertrand.marquis@arm.com>
References: <55d56a174a0f04520d4a1558630bb0b739074b13.1776946505.git.bertrand.marquis@arm.com>
From: Bertrand Marquis <bertrand.marquis@arm.com>
Date: Thu, 16 Apr 2026 19:30:47 +0200
Subject: [RFC PATCH 23/28] hw/virtio: add virtio-msg linux bridge backend

Add the linux bridge backend that connects virtio-msg requests to the
host bridge device and maintains dynamic DMA map state.

Implement realize, reset, runtime paths, property handling, and build
wiring under hw/virtio for the bridge backend.

Fold the bridge log ownership and reduced trace surface into this patch
so backend diagnostics land in their final RFC form.

Signed-off-by: Bertrand Marquis <bertrand.marquis@arm.com>
---
 hw/virtio/Kconfig                   |    6 +
 hw/virtio/meson.build               |    2 +
 hw/virtio/trace-events              |    6 +
 hw/virtio/virtio-msg-linux-bridge.c | 3366 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 include/hw/virtio/virtio-msg-prot.h |    2 +
 include/hw/virtio/virtio-msg.h      |  128 +
 6 files changed, 3510 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 hw/virtio/virtio-msg-linux-bridge.c

